---
layout: base
title: Search
description: "Search all Ahvantir lore articles."
permalink: /search/
---

<div class="page-header">
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="page-title">Search the records</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">{{ collections.allArticles.length }} articles across {{ meta.categories.length }} subjects.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container search-page">
  <div id="search" class="pagefind-search"></div>
  <noscript>
    <p class="search-noscript">Search requires JavaScript. <a href="/articles/">Browse all articles instead →</a></p>
  </noscript>

  {# Before anything is typed this page was a single input on an otherwise
     empty screen, with the footer pulled up under it -- which reads as a page
     that failed to load rather than one waiting for input. These are ways in
     for a reader who does not yet know what to ask for. search.js hides the
     whole block as soon as there is a query, so it never competes with
     results. #}
  <div class="search-start" id="search-start">
    <section class="search-start__block">
      <h2 class="search-start__title">Browse by subject</h2>
      <div class="search-start__subjects">
        {% for cat in meta.categories %}
        <a href="/articles/#{{ cat.slug }}" class="subject-chip" style="--cat-color: {{ cat.color }}">
          <span class="subject-chip__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                 stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">{{ cat.icon | safe }}</svg>
          </span>
          {{ cat.label }}
        </a>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="search-start__block">
      <h2 class="search-start__title">Or go somewhere</h2>
      <ul class="search-start__links" role="list">
        <li><a href="/articles/arumas/">Aru&rsquo;Mas</a> <span>the city these records are written from</span></li>
        <li><a href="/timeline/">The historical record</a> <span>founding era to the present day</span></li>
        <li><a href="/map/">The world map</a> <span>the archipelago and its districts</span></li>
        <li><a href="/almanac/">The almanac</a> <span>calendar, suns, moons and sky</span></li>
        <li><a href="/graph/">Relations</a> <span>how people, places and powers connect</span></li>
        <li><a href="/recently-added/">Recently added</a> <span>what has changed lately</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>

{% block scripts %}
<link href="/pagefind/pagefind-ui.css" rel="stylesheet">
<script src="/pagefind/pagefind-ui.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/search.js"></script>
{% endblock %}
